					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coil780" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1454221); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1454221&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609923836" alt="coil780" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1454221)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/coil780" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1454221); return false;" >coil780</a></span> <span class="odate time_1354247089 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Nov 2012 03:44</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1632667">
									

<p>Can't get behind this, for a lot of small reasons.</p>
<ul>
<li>There are just enough issues with tone and grammar to be noticeable as an issue overall. For instance,
<ul>
<li>&quot;Under no circumstances may personnel approach within 30m of SCP-1275 if it is loose, recontainment will be accomplished via specialized capture netting, delivered by air.&quot; Run-on sentence, first comma should be a period or semicolon.</li>
<li>Mixed usage of &quot;re-containment&quot; and &quot;recontainment.&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;Affected by gravity, yet registers no weight.&quot; That's what gravity <em>is</em>.</li>
<li>&quot;the object will vanish to parts unknown.&quot; Bad tone.</li>
<li>&quot;Hostilities began, containment was breached.&quot; Poor tone, bad comma.</li>
<li>The text to re-collapse the two collapsibles are inconsistent: <em>-Hide</em> vs <em>- hide block</em>.</li>
<li>etc.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>The recovery log is one paragraph of recovery log followed by two unrelated to its recovery: the second paragraph is about its inferred or deduced behavior prior to containment, while the third is about the Foundation's exploratory interactions with it after containment.</li>
<li>The recovery log says &quot;the entity sides with or is controlled by <em>the</em> hostile agents&quot; (emphasis mine), but you haven't yet introduced any hostile agents except to suggest that SCP-1275 may be &quot;controlled by an outside intelligence.&quot; Did you originally have the Incident Report and Recovery Log swapped?</li>
<li>&quot;Internal breach efforts&quot; by whom? SCP-1275 or the &quot;enemy agents&quot;?</li>
<li>The Incident Log is not about a single incident, but instead comprises over 19 months of behavior including at least four or five unique events worthy of being called &quot;incidents.&quot;</li>
</ul>
<p>In particular, the back half of this piece reads more like a story/tale than a containment document, and the escalation of hostilities feels like <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-1322">SCP-1322</a> but not as well done.</p>

							</div>

								
