				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609923836" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;" >SoullessSingularity</a></span> <span class="odate time_1354248834 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Nov 2012 04:13</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1632689">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Click&nbsp;for&nbsp;Full&nbsp;Review</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Full&nbsp;Review</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Under no circumstances may personnel approach within 30m of SCP-1275 if it is loose, recontainment will be accomplished via specialized capture netting, delivered by air</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a really awkward sentence. It really is. Could do with some fixing, preferably something about the comma between 'if it is loose' and 'recontainment'.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1275 seems not to exist fully within the material world.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems like quite a logical jump when you think about it, especially so much if it's considered important enough to mention in the beginning of the description.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Parts separated from the main body appear to flow extradimensionally</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;extradimensionally? That sounds so cheesed. Hell, even 'through an unknown means' would be better than that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>objects of value</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is extremely vague. Value according to whom? If I thought that my dog was valuable, would it be enveloped too? Valuable to the Foundation? So D-class would be ignored?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>will vanish to parts unknown</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This also seems really really cheesed and iffy tone. You could better state that they have vanished without any successful recovery thus far, or something.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the object enveloped<br />
Objects and personnel taken</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I see that this is inconsistent. If you're going to call them 'the objects enveloped' stick to that.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>However, evidence now suggests that SCP-1275 has an end point in another part of the world that it is connected to extradimensionally, and that it shifts portions of itself between these endpoints, accounting for its apparent fluctuations in volume.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Subtle as a brick to the face. I also have no idea how any evidence could suggest this. I mean, jesus hell man. If that evidence existed, it would be more fun to have it put in the article in a way that the reader could infer it than having it slammed into them like this. Also, I am becoming progressively more and more unimpressed with this article and have yet to see why it would be a keter.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The entity appears unable to remove the endpoint held by the foundation. It is theorized that either this is the primary half of the entity, or that it naturally has a divided existence.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;What? The Foundation has an endpoint? This wasn't mentioned in the beginning of the description at all? So confused. What do you mean remove? Like, pick it up and move it around? What is the endpoint?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>deemed to be of value</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&#8230;By who? By it? It has knowledge of the Foundation? This isn't mentioned as to how it could acquire this information? It's not even registered as through an unknown means?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>presumably transporting them to its other endpoint</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What evidence is there for that claim? I just don't get it at this point and it sounds very thrown-together.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Evidence</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What evidence? It sounds so cheesed right now.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the entity sides with</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Uhm&#8230; I don't like this tone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>is controlled by the hostile agents</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What hostile agents? Hostile agents were mentioned in the article? Am I reading this wrong?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>To date too little data has been recovered to establish a definite link to any individual group.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't understand, this link to a random hostile group comes out of nowhere.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>though apparently none to itself</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The fact it can 'disgorge' high energy explosives should be an important fact mentioned in the description, methinks. I mean, that is fairly important.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Entity was moved</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Oh come on, not even 'the' now? I don't approve. I also have an issue with the whole 'the entity'. I would much prefer it to be more 'SCP-XXXX' in there, or something. If it's like multiple sentences in a row of SCP-XXXX, that's fine to replace one with 'the entity', but instead we have the exact opposite problem in which 'the entity' is refered to again and again.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An unknown hostile retrieval team</p>
</blockquote>
<p>OH! THERE THE HOSTILE AGENTS ARE! Why wasn't this explained previously? Why would you confuse the reader by specifying things that aren't even gone into until later in the article, but refuse to put in big details like BEING ABLE TO DISGORGE EXPLOSIVES AND SCPS in the description?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>enemy agents armed with paranormal weaponry emerged from within SCP-1275</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wait, so, are we talking about these hostile agents or the other hostile agents? Also, what idiot thinks that's a good idea? This isn't a video game, you don't just set up base in the enemy's base and expect it to work.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>driven back into SCP-1275 again</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It was driven back previously? Also, 'driven back' seems like very odd tone.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The mesh grid has prevented SCP-1275 from disgorging objects capable of breaching its containment</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The fact that the SCP not only disgorges objects, but is prevented from doing so by a mesh grid seems like something that would be included in the description rather than vague allusions to ~mysterious enemy agents~ and ~a portal to another part of the world~ that isn't made clear or even explained until the last few bits. Honestly, even a (refer to Addendum-XXXX-BUTT) would've been better to the lack any explanation or warning whatsoever.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>has thus far prevented transmitters from signaling its location to enemy agents</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wait, how do we know this? Does it have transmitters? Not sure about the whole 'enemy agents' thing now that I think about it too.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, it seems like a very confused article. Important details are specified in the beginning without context and then the context is shoved into the addendum in the kind of forced manner that resembles &quot;&#8230;and then he woke up&quot;. There are multiple important details about what the object does that aren't at all mentioned in the description, which is a problem for me. I also find issue with multiple pieces of tone and sentence structures. Overall, don't like the article. I think that the &quot;reveal&quot; is actually really cool, and the idea of some organization purposefully trying to sabotage the Foundation from within also cool. But its badly organized right now and me liking for what you were trying to do is outweighed by my dislike of how you did it.</p>

							</div>

										<div class="signature">
					<hr class="signature-separator"/>
					

<p>Living the dream, or dreaming the life?</p>

				</div>
					
					
